<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">About LifeLink SL</div><h1 class="section-title">A Sri Lankan academic prototype for donor and hospital coordination.</h1><p class="section-sub">LifeLink SL was created to reduce the effort required to reach suitable registered donors and to keep emergency coordination visible in one place. It complements, rather than replaces, official blood-bank and healthcare processes.</p><div class="grid-2 mt-2"><div class="card"><h3>What the system does</h3><ul><li>Registers and verifies volunteer donor accounts.</li><li>Coordinates urgent blood requests and donor responses.</li><li>Escalates unresolved requests to wider donors and hospitals.</li><li>Supports campaigns, prototype inventory transfers, QR verification and reporting.</li></ul></div><div class="card"><h3>What the system does not do</h3><ul><li>It does not replace NBTS or hospital blood-bank systems.</li><li>It does not store detailed patient medical records.</li><li>It does not decide medical eligibility or blood compatibility.</li><li>It does not perform transplant allocation or clinical organ matching.</li></ul></div></div></div></section>
